Z||000000||Htown86GT||08-16-2001||08:08 AM||||Left your keys in the trunk and have waited so long that the battery is dead..<P>Any Ideas on how to get the key?<BR>Of course battery is not accessable.||||reg||3
Z||000001||Tigger||08-16-2001||08:14 AM||||I hope this is one of those hypothetical "what if" questions.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||85SE||08-16-2001||08:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Htown86GT:<BR><B>Any Ideas on how to get the key?<BR>Of course battery is not accessable.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Htown86GT: theogre has a little piece on this in his cave - read the bottom of the page on his site called "Trunk Latch" on the Electrical menu.  <P>Hope this helps!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Andrew Menchions - 85SE - AKA Fieroless in Newfoundland||||reg||3
Z||000003||Wolfhound||08-16-2001||08:39 AM||||Take a hypothetic lenght of two strand regular house wiring. Strip the outer insulation 12 to 14 inches back. Strip only about an 1/8th  inch on the black and white wire. Use this to jump to the hypothetic battery through the vent and screen. You can get enough contact to operate the deck latch. Takes two hypothetic people to make it easy. One has to hold the wire in contact with the battery terminals. Once open you can jump or charge properly.<P>Hypotheticly, that is!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-16-2001||09:36 AM||||take a length of cord with a male cig plug on it. connect the wire ends to another battery, plug it into your cig lighter socket and hit the button.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Urchin||08-16-2001||09:43 AM||||Make a spare set of keys<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_3.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-16-2001||09:58 AM||||Take *two* cigarette lighter plugs. Wire them + to + and - to -. Plug one in the lighter socket of the Fiero, and the other in the lighter of another car. <BR>If the lighter fuse is blown, this will not work.<BR>(I have seen this setup for sale, somewhere.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
